const e=`Despite the many advantages of Artificial Intelligence, *many risks* also emerge. Deepfake technology, which uses AI to create fake images and videos, has raised serious concerns. These false representations can be used to mislead the public and distort reality. It is important to remain cautious and recognize that the images and videos we see may not be real.

**Challenge:** You will see a mix of images generated by artificial intelligence (AI) and real photographs. Your goal is to identify the fake ones. You can use your powers of observation and your knowledge to spot the differences, but as you will find, this can be very difficult. By training a model for this problem, you will be able to achieve much higher accuracy.

**Image Sources:** All images are either computer-generated via the website [thispersondoesnotexist.com](https://thispersondoesnotexist.com) using the *StyleGAN* software, or real photographs from the FFHQ (Flickr-Faces-HQ) dataset, which includes Creative Commons photos and public-domain images.
`;export{e as default};
